<!--
  The same four cells for Android 13+ themed icons — same geometry as ic_launcher_foreground, see
  the note there for why the span is 62 and how it was computed.

  ONE DIFFERENCE, AND IT IS DELIBERATE: THE FADE IS FLATTENED TO SOLID.

  A monochrome layer is a mask — the system supplies the colour from the user's wallpaper theme and
  keeps only our alpha. The colour version's 30 / 52 / 76 / 100% ramp is what makes the row read as
  an acceleration, but on a tinted ground the two faintest cells disappear, and a four-cell mark
  missing its first two is just a bar and a dash. The design that specifies this mark flags exactly
  that and supplies a solid variant for the themed layer.

  Flattening costs less than it looks. The lengths alone carry the meaning: 5 -> 9 -> 14 -> 22 still
  accelerates into the hold without any help from opacity.

  Kept as its own file rather than aliasing the foreground, because that one names a colour resource
  and a themed icon must not carry any of the app's own colour into the user's palette.
-->
